  "narrative": "No validation request is made because the independent-validation budget is exhausted. I interpreted all estimates as already signed to the registered direction. For H280-H285, direction -1 means a positive signed mean difference indicates that PTEN-loss cells have a more negative, stronger STAT3 dependency score than PTEN-intact cells in the named context. H280, low IFN-gamma signature, shows a clear positive effect, +0.209, 95% CI 0.133 to 0.285, with adequate cells, so I accept it as a within-dataset consistency finding; it does not prove causality or generalizability and may reflect confounding between PTEN loss, IFN state, PI3K pathway state, or other genomic features. H281, high aneuploidy, also supports the effect, +0.201, 95% CI 0.092 to 0.310; this is somewhat wider and consistent with less precise estimation, but the interval excludes zero. This should not be confused with an interaction claim, because H270 did not support stronger PTEN effect specifically versus lower-aneuploidy cells. H282 and H283 accept low- and high-serum contexts: +0.239, CI 0.157 to 0.320, and +0.291, CI 0.216 to 0.366, respectively. These support media-context internal consistency but not causal media effects. H284, batch_a, gives +0.212, CI 0.097 to 0.326, which is positive but less precise; it supports presence of the effect in one technical batch without establishing batch causality or ruling out batch correlation. H285, high mutation burden, gives +0.277, CI 0.184 to 0.370, again internally supportive. Taken together, H280-H285 increase confidence in the PTEN-loss/STAT3-dependency association within this dataset, especially because the main accepted PTEN-STAT3 contrast remains internally coherent across many technical and biological strata. However, these are still discovery subgroup contrasts with multiplicity and correlated predictors, and PTEN-STAT3 remains the only accepted main association lacking independent validation. For H50, the MTAP-loss interaction on MDM2 dependency by TP53 loss is +0.030, 95% CI -0.039 to 0.0999. This is directionally positive but not statistically supported; the interval includes zero and remains wide enough that a small-to-moderate positive interaction cannot be cleanly excluded. Therefore I leave H50 unresolved rather than rejecting a positive modification, but close it for this dataset because the prior TP53-loss MDM2 main effect was itself null and no validation budget remains.",
  "research_notes": "Final appraise update. Validation budget is exhausted, so no new independent validation was requested. PTEN-loss/STAT3-dependency robustness checks H280-H285 all gave positive signed mean differences with 95% intervals excluding zero: low IFN +0.209, high aneuploidy +0.201, low serum +0.239, high serum +0.291, batch_a +0.212, high mutation burden +0.277. They are accepted as deferred within-dataset context supports, not causal or externally generalizable findings. H50, MTAP-loss modification of TP53-loss MDM2 interaction, is +0.030 with CI -0.039 to 0.0999, directionally positive but inconclusive; it is unresolved and closed. Core accepted within-dataset associations: MSI-high stronger WRN dependency; SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency; KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency; TP53-loss weaker USP7 dependency; CDKN2A-loss stronger MDM2 dependency; PTEN-loss stronger STAT3 dependency. PTEN-STAT3 remains the only accepted main association without independent validation. Most other driver, marker, DNA-repair, cell-cycle, pathway, and interaction hypotheses are null, inconsistent, underpowered, or unsupported."
